Zero boot capacity expansion to448KiB
Verification date:2026-11-16

Original Zero sources compiled with the own capacity candidate compiler:
bios.zero, loader.zero, loader32.zero, image.zero, iso.zero.
BIOS14149 bytes, EFI64 14848 bytes, EFI32 21504 bytes. Existing fixed boot
component bounds remain16KiB/64KiB/64KiB. No full project build was performed
by this task; root owns integration of the new network/window code.

Capacity contract
Each padded kernel is458752 bytes (112 EFI pages,896 FAT clusters).
BIOS loads14 separate32KiB requests to20000..8ffff, with conventional RAM
at least576KiB and a nonzero EBDA boundary no lower than90000. The BIOS
handoff reports112 pages. Its E820-validated pool and framebuffer policy
remain unchanged. IA32 EFI validates code base no higher thanfff8f000,
retaining the same top4KiB address guard. Both EFI loaders reject files
outside1..458752 and retain bounded short-read handling.

FAT input length is1048576 bytes; output remains16777216 bytes. Kernel chains
are260..1155 and1156..2051. Data ends at sector2338; free area starts2339.
ISO input length is17711104 bytes; output8680*2048=17776640 bytes. Optical
extents are BIOS32..39, kernel64 40..263, kernel32 264..487, EFI488..8679.
Directory sizes, paired-endian quantities and EFI catalog LBA all agree.

Executed checks
2115 assertions passed, including individual bounded FAT-chain traversal.
All four FAT payloads and all four ISO payloads extract byte-identically.
Both FAT copies match; unused FAT/data areas remain free/zero. ISO directory
and volume sizes have correct endian pairs. El Torito validation checksum,
BIOS LBA32/load32 and EFI LBA488/load32768 are exact.
Both writers passed exact input, one-byte short/excess input, invalid header,
unreadable input descriptor and /dev/full output status checks.

Four private whole-slot VM probes passed and exited:
BIOS64; BIOS32 with long mode and PAE disabled; AMD64 OVMF; IA32 OVMF.
All used QEMU pc/TCG,128MiB RAM and no writable data disk. Each probe verified
markers at offsets131071,131072,262143,262144,393215,393216 and458751, code
pages112, the full64KiB arena and its loader-owned stack pool. The same probe
ISO SHA256 isae07d14ca94379ba248be55dc887c69067a18d994c8430d7e15f410c59358daa.
This is complete-capacity evidence, not a final network-kernel boot claim.

External read-only inspectors
fsck.fat -n exited0:7 files,2050/32479 clusters.
xorriso exited0:8680 data blocks, El Torito BIOS at32 and UEFI at488,
and the four expected root files. Inspectors did not construct the image.

Preservation and limits
Original build/zero.iso remained8d494eca3adbf8998b1674d4d7c4cd03308f40ba87ee3213a806fefa6c9f7d31.
build/data.img remainedc730241fb30f5516867c751006951a2878f360319195ee975411a05f040f27e8.
build/data.vdi remained7f58fb36c934405757da797ca65f2dddef3858e69107f43e2cae59d14c89bc5f.
These original disks were never attached. No native VirtualBox or physical
hardware result is claimed. The new memory-bound predicates were reviewed;
the current run did not inject firmware BDA/EBDA failure values. Historical
low-RAM refusal evidence remains separate under boot-growth-0.7.0.

